5 Fragments
incremental: true already fragments every bullet list. Everything else needs an explicit class.
Text appears on click. {.fragment}

![](img.png){.fragment width=50%}

::: {.fragment}
block appears on click
:::

::: {.fragment fragment-index=2}
appears second even if written first
:::

Word {.fragment .highlight-red fragment-index=1}

fragment-index shares numbering across the whole slide; equal indices appear together.
Fragment effects: .fade-in (default), .fade-out, .fade-up, .fade-in-then-out, .fade-in-then-semi-out, .grow, .shrink, .strike, .highlight-red, .highlight-blue, .highlight-green, .highlight-current-red, .semi-fade-out.
Non-incremental list on an incremental deck:

::: {.nonincremental}
- shows all at once
- second item
:::

Pause marker inside a paragraph or list: a line containing only . . ..
{.nofragment} is not a revealjs class; it does nothing. Use .nonincremental.

6 Transitions
Deck default is fade. Per slide:
# Title {transition="slide"}
# Title {transition="slide-in fade-out"}
# Title {transition="zoom" transition-speed="fast"}
# Title {background-transition="zoom"}
Values: none, fade, slide, convex, concave, zoom. Speed: default, fast, slow. Transitions are ignored in PDF export and in ?view=scroll.

7 Auto-animate
Consecutive slides with the same title and auto-animate=true; elements with matching data-id move/resize between them.
# Desk analogy {auto-animate=true}

&lt;div data-id="box" style="width:100px; height:100px; background:#5e81ac;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

# Desk analogy {auto-animate=true}

&lt;div data-id="box" style="width:300px; height:100px; background:#bf616a;"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

Text elements auto-match by content if no data-id.
Options on the slide: auto-animate-easing="ease-in-out", auto-animate-duration=1.5, auto-animate-unmatched=false.
Auto-animate ignores the deck transition for those slides.

11 Callouts, asides, speaker notes
::: {.callout-note}
Text. Types: note | tip | warning | important | caution
:::

::: {.callout-tip title="Custom title" collapse=true}
:::

::: {.aside}
Small text at the bottom of the slide (footnote-style).
:::

::: {.notes}
Speaker notes. Visible only in speaker view (press S).
:::
Callouts are large in revealjs; {.callout-note .smaller} or an inline style helps.

12 Shortcodes
{{&lt; countdown "10:00" &gt;}}
{{&lt; countdown minutes=5 seconds=0 &gt;}}
{{&lt; countdown minutes=5 top=0 right=0 font_size="2em" &gt;}}
{{&lt; qrcode https://URL colorDark='#0011bb' &gt;}}
{{&lt; qrcode https://URL width=150 height=150 &gt;}}
{{&lt; meta date-modified &gt;}}
{{&lt; meta title &gt;}}

Countdown starts on click; space bar pauses it. Positions: top, bottom, left, right in px.
To show a shortcode literally (e.g. in a code block) write it with triple braces, otherwise it is executed.
Install once per project: quarto add gadenbuie/countdown/quarto, quarto add jmbuhr/quarto-qrcode. They live in _extensions/ which must be committed.

15 Backgrounds
# Title {background-color="#2e3440"}
# Title {background-image="img.png" background-size="contain"}
# Title {background-image="img.png" background-opacity=0.3}
# Title {background-video="clip.mp4" background-video-loop=true background-video-muted=true}
# Title {background-iframe="URL" background-interactive=true}
Dark background: text stays #3b4252 from custom.css, so add &lt;div style="color:#eceff4"&gt; or use {.dark}-style inline overrides.
